domain SEMANTIC_TARGET_ASSERTION:
  description "Correct an unsupported invalid-grammar expectation while retaining legacy response refusal."
evidence FAILURE:
  "Only the old targetDefinitionSchema circular-reference assertion fails in the migration grammar revision case. Earlier assertion that old responseSchema is circular passes; corrected responseSchema is valid and distinct."
evidence SOURCE:
  "Read character-migration-prompts.ts: old target schema is native zodResponseFormat(CharacterDefinitionV3Schema), modern target uses duplicate-default repair helper. Generic recursive JSON remains in migration operation response, not inherently in target definition. Current target native grammar passes assertXaiResponseSchema. Test conflates target grammar with operation response grammar."
premise ALTERNATIVES:
  "A response refusal regression is ruled out by the earlier passing assert. No current contract requires an invalid target definition schema; making a valid schema invalid would violate repair purpose. Historical stored payload hash conformance is not established by this test, so no such claim is made. Exact past introducing commit remains uninspected."
premise BOUNDS:
  "Retain old prompt branch, no auto upgrade, old response rejection and corrected response distinction. Change only old target schema assertion from throws to doesNotThrow; current target validity stays. No provider call, source behavior, migration authority or frozen saved request changes. Owner all-tests repair scope and Accepted ADR0030 migration constraints govern."
decision D1 based_on FAILURE, SOURCE, ALTERNATIVES, BOUNDS:
  "Audit then correct this test expectation to reflect actual separate grammar roles, rerun migration regression and backend types, preserve source-diverged verification until reviewed Seal refresh."
